    "created_at": "2018-08-10T01:12:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-10T01:12:23Z",
    "body": "It should be fine. I don't know the event dispatching process too well, but could it be possible that when \"firing an event at the `Window` object with *legacy target override flag* set\", event listeners registered on another object were also invoked? I'm guessing no, but it happened to be true then merely checking if the `Window` object has an `unload` event listener wouldn't been enough… (`body.onload` doesn't count, as the event _listener_ is registered on `Window` still.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
